{
  "case_id": "2022-22-49",
  "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in Case 22-49, Lora versus United States. Mr. Rosenberg."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Lawrence D. Rosenberg)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Subsection 924(j) does not include or incorporate a bar against concurrent sentences."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you do with the government's argument that seems to suggest that it's simply an accumulation of the penalties, an aggregation or an increase of the penalties under (c)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can I ask you a -- a question about section (c)(1)(C), capital C --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so the government can charge even a death under (c) if it doesn't intend to seek the death penalty?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, in that situation, is the person convicted under (j) and 1112 or just under (j)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Ross (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 924(j) sweeps in all of subsection (c)'s provisions. It does not, as my friend suggests, pick and choose particular factual elements."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Ross (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 924(j) then incorporates -- then requires that the court consider whether to add additional punishment for the homicide."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you do with the language in 924(c) that refers to sentences -- it says notwithstanding any other provision of law, no sentence imposed on a person under this subsection."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, but why is that, Ms. Ross? I mean, suppose that (j) had not said in the course of a violation of subsection (c) but just repeated all of subsection (c)'s language. Then what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is correct, isn't it, that under your theory, subparagraph (c)(5)(B) is superfluous?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Isn't the truth of the matter here that Congress just made a mistake?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0001-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I -- can I go back to the absurdity point?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: I'm asking how the Court looks at -- not -- at (j), not 924(c). What -- why is it absurd for a Congress that is enacting (j) to have had a separate penalty structure that did not incorporate the mandatory minimums of (c) but instead took care of that circumstance through, as the text says here, giving the death penalty, increasing the maximums and the like?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. ROSS: So I think we might well take that course, Justice Kagan, again, because I think that's sort of the natural consequence of treating the (j) as not incorporating the (c) penalties."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: But that's not the Blockburger test. I don't understand. So you're -- you're suddenly now asking us as a result of this case to revisit Blockburger and what it says about when there are separate offenses?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: Isn't --isn't the only"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(j) situation involves a death, my question is, under what circumstance is a court actually going to go below the five years?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Lawrence D. Rosenberg",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I just have five brief -- excuse me, brief points. First of all, my friend on the government's side admits that we don't know what Congress's intent really was."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-49",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ec6f697a0eb7197e7ddeb53116fdea2d718d0f0d69aae81edd75a7676333ee8c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ec6f697a0eb7-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:28 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
